 "definition": "IBM's command set for controlling its printers, also supported by some other makers' printers in an emulation mode.",
 "description": {
  "text": "A family of page description languages used by IBM printers, covering Proprinter, Quietwriter, Quickwriter and LaserPrinter commands. Introduced in 1981 and renamed PPDS in 1989, it has upward-compatible function levels; many laser and inkjet printers do not support it.",
